{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "logs": {
        "text": "php://stderr",
        "summary": "build/infection-summary.log"
    },
    // RedisStorage/ApcuStorage are covered by the Integration suite (#[Covers],
    // not #[CoversNothing] - the latter zeroes mutation attribution entirely).
    // Needs REDIS_HOST + ext-apcu (apc.enable_cli=1) reachable, or their MSI drops.
    //
    // The remaining survivors are all in ApcuStorage and are equivalent or
    // environment-only mutants:
    //  - isAvailable() `&&` -> `||`: only distinguishable when ext-apcu is
    //    loaded but apc.enable_cli is off, a state the test environments do
    //    not construct;
    //  - lock()'s `random_int(1, PHP_INT_MAX)` bounds and the retry loop's
    //    `$attempt = 0` / `<` bounds: shift the token range or the spin budget
    //    by one iteration, externally unobservable;
    //  - lock()'s `usleep()` and the `apcu_store()` that refreshes the lease
    //    after a successful CAS, plus unlock()'s `apcu_cas()`: dropping them
    //    changes contention timing and lease length, not the outcome any
    //    single-process assertion can observe. Real contention IS exercised by
    //    neverAdmitsMoreProbesThanProbeLimitUnderRealForkContention, but pcov
    //    coverage does not propagate out of pcntl_fork()'d children back to the
    //    parent report, so infection never selects that test for these mutants
    //    (the same phenomenon rasuvaeff/bulkhead documents for
    //    ApcuBulkheadStore::lock).
    //
    // Internal\BreakerState (the transition logic shared by InMemoryStorage
    // and ApcuStorage, see AGENTS.md golden rule 3) carries #[Covers] on
    // InMemoryStorageTest as of the ER-003 mutation-coverage audit (2026-08-02).
    // Seven of its mutants are equivalent - `entry['probeSuccesses']`/
    // `entry['probeSlots']` are only ever READ while `state === HalfOpen`, and
    // the only way INTO HalfOpen is either `admit()`'s `Open -> HalfOpen`
    // transition (which unconditionally resets both fields to 0, discarding
    // whatever they held) or `forceState()` (which always starts from a fresh
    // `BreakerState::fresh()` entry, never from a prior entry's leftover
    // fields) - so a `0 -> -1` mutant on a write that happens while LEAVING
    // HalfOpen is dead by construction, never a write exposed via `fresh()`
    // itself (that one IS observable through forceState() and is covered by
    // forceStateToHalfOpenStartsWithNoOccupiedProbeSlotsOrSuccesses):
    //  - BreakerState.php:252 `probeSuccesses = 0` (HalfOpen -> Closed, probe
    //    succeeded) and :253 `probeSlots = 0` in the same branch;
    //  - BreakerState.php:260 `probeSuccesses = 0` (HalfOpen -> Open, probe
    //    failed) and :261 `probeSlots = 0` in the same branch.
    // BreakerState.php:84 `$entry['probeSlots'] > 0` -> `>= 0` (probe-lease
    // expiry check): at `probeSlots === 0` both the `>` and `>=` variants take
    // branches that produce the IDENTICAL result (`probeSlots = 0`,
    // `probeGenerationAt = $now`) - `probeSlots` is never legitimately
    // negative, so the two conditions only ever diverge on unreachable state.
    // (BreakerState.php:243's `max(0, $entry['probeSlots'] - 1)` floor looked
    // equivalent under the "exactly once recordOutcome()" contract, but is
    // NOT - a caller that releases the same probe twice (a real, if
    // contract-violating, bug) drives it negative without the clamp; killed
    // by doubleReleasingAProbeSlotNeverLeavesItNegative.)
    // BreakerState.php:213 `count($entry['ring']) > $ratio->window()` -> `>=`:
    // trimming an array that already has exactly `window()` elements to its
    // last `window()` elements is a no-op (`array_slice($ring, -N)` on an
    // N-element list returns the same N elements) - the two conditions only
    // diverge on a boundary where the "extra" trim changes nothing.
    // BreakerState.php:218 removing `array_values()` around the `within`
    // eviction `array_filter()`: nothing downstream of `$entry['ring']`
    // (BreakerState.php, InMemoryStorage.php, ApcuStorage.php) ever indexes it
    // by a specific integer key - every consumer is `count()`/`array_filter()`/
    // `array_slice()` (all key-order-agnostic) or a subsequent `[] =` append
    // (key-gap-tolerant) - so a non-reindexed (gappy) array is behaviorally
    // identical to a reindexed one for every reachable caller.
    //
    // minMsi dropped 97 -> 96 in the ER-003 audit (2026-08-02): closing the
    // #[Covers] attribution gap grew the mutant denominator from 333 to 442
    // (109 new mutants, 105 of them in BreakerState, the package's most
    // branch-dense file - see docs/evolved-rules.md ER-003). The honest
    // ceiling after killing everything killable is ~96.8-97.1% depending on
    // which side of the pre-existing ApcuStorage.php:235 escape/timeout flake
    // (documented above) a given run lands on - 96 leaves margin for that
    // flake without hiding a real gap.
    "testFramework": "testo",
    "minMsi": 96,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
